.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELLTYPE> void \fBcsmp::PDE_Integrator_CRM\fP< dim, CELLTYPE >::IntegrateOver (\fBModelSubDomain\fP< dim, CELLTYPE > & domain, bool debug = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
accumulates, assembles, and solves PDEs in domain of interest; 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdebug\fP prompts output of solution matrices to file; uses node numbering
.RE
.PP
Assembly and solution of the system of linear algebraic equations, but without consideration of boundary integrals:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
Dimensionsing of the solution matrix (n-variables, scalar or vector etc\&.)
.IP "2." 4
Accumulation of the FE or FV integrals
.IP "3." 4
Multiplication of the initial conditions into the RHS in the case of the transient problem\&.
.IP "4." 4
Late accumulation to RHS
.IP "5." 4
Essential conditions (either with or without elimination of the Dirichlet constraints from the matrix)\&.
.IP "6." 4
Output matrix and vectors to get diagnostics
.IP "7." 4
Solution
.IP "8." 4
Output results back to moel
.IP "9." 4
Postprocessing (if respective pde operators were added to the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP) and writing related results to model\&. 
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELLTYPE> void \fBcsmp::PDE_Integrator_CRM\fP< dim, CELLTYPE >::LateAccumulate (const \fBModelSubDomain\fP< dim, CELLTYPE > & gref)\fR [protected]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
accumulates finite-element integrals to matrix and vector after the corresponding entries were already multiplied with the initial conditions; uses node numbering \fBLateAccumulate()\fP adds source and sink terms into the righthand vector after all other accumulations have occurred\&. This timing is required if an implicit time-stepping scheme is used\&. The method retrieves information from the mesh and the property managers\&. If a group computation is carried out, the target group is accessed by a pointer\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Those math operators which have been ear-marked for late accumulation are added by this method\&. Like in \fBAccumulate()\fP this addition requires the execution of the math operator methods:

.PP
.PP
.nf
GetOperands();
ComputeContribution();
AssignToGlobal();
.fi
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
\fBLateAccumulate()\fP is executed only in time-dependent calculations\&. The execution is invoked internally, when the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP is passed to the \fBModel\fP\&. 
.PP
.nf
@attention Method relies on a 0\&.\&.n contiguous numbering of the finite element nodes\&.

.fi
.PP
 
